{"id": "unknown-2026-07-17-005", "date": "2026-07-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.75, "keywords": ["decline", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "US cotton export sales slump to marketing-year low despite demand", "content": "US Upland cotton export sales fell to the lowest level of the current marketing year in the week ended July 9, dropping 48 per cent from the previous week, while export shipments also declined.\nIn contrast, Pima cotton sales strengthened further, led by India, although Pima export shipments weakened, indicating softer near-term US cotton demand.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/us-cotton-export-sales-slump-to-marketing-year-low-despite-demand-311831-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-17-006", "date": "2026-07-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["order_visibility", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["increase", "loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Switzerland’s Rieter sees strong orders after Barmag acquisition", "content": "Rieter's H1 2026 order intake rose 56 per cent to CHF 554.1 million (~$703.7 million), driven by the Barmag acquisition, while sales increased 72 per cent to CHF 576.7 million.\nThe group reported a net loss of CHF 54.9 million (~$69.7 million) amid integration and financing costs but reaffirmed its 2026 outlook and advanced textile recycling through a new partnership with recycling powerhouse", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/switzerland-s-rieter-sees-strong-orders-after-barmag-acquisition-311818-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-17-007", "date": "2026-07-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "order_visibility", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "ICE cotton drops on weaker export sales, profit booking", "content": "ICE cotton futures fell to a multi-week low, with the December 2026 contract dropping 2.76 per cent to 79.30 cents per pound after weak US export sales triggered profit booking.\nA stronger US dollar and broad commodity market weakness added pressure, while traders continued to monitor China's reserve auction, US weather, and tightening ICE-certified cotton stocks.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-drops-on-weaker-export-sales-profit-booking-311819-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-17-008", "date": "2026-07-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["sustainable_textile", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bharat Tex 2026 Day 3 highlights innovation and sustainability", "content": "Bharat Tex 2026's third day focused on circularity, sustainable sourcing, financing, skills and technology to strengthen India's textile industry.\nDiscussions brought together policymakers, global brands, investors and industry leaders, while Madhya Pradesh promoted its textile investment potential.\nSessions also emphasised traceability, ESG compliance and export competitiveness.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bharat-tex-2026-day-3-highlights-innovation-and-sustainability-311816-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-17-009", "date": "2026-07-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bharat Tex 2026 backs global growth for Indian apparel brands", "content": "Indian textile and apparel brands discussed international scaling at Bharat Tex 2026, with export performance and 2030 targets framing the opportunity.\nThe session focused on converting manufacturing strength into design-led, culturally distinctive retail growth. \nQuality, sustainability, traceability, craft heritage and omnichannel reach emerged as priorities for global competitiveness. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bharat-tex-2026-backs-global-growth-for-indian-apparel-brands-311826-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
